[85] **5. Dust supply lets a donation inflate the yield index past overflow**

`AbstractToken._accrueGlobalYield` · Confidence: 85

**Description**
An attacker with one wei of supply donates a flash loan, so accYieldPerToken reaches 1e51 and later keep-split holders and yieldAccrued overflow.

Trace on a fresh 18-decimal (WXDAI/sDAI) instance: mint 1 wei (or mint 1e18 then burn 1e18-1) so `totalSupply == 1`; `setYieldSplit(10000)`; flash-borrow 1e24 WXDAI, deposit into sDAI and transfer the shares to the token; `claimKeptYield(receiver)` runs `_accrueGlobalYield` with `acc += 1e24 * 1e27 / 1 = 1e51` and credits the attacker `kept = 1e24`, which is minted to the receiver and burned to repay the loan. Cost is the flash fee. `accYieldPerToken` only grows and no function resets it. Afterwards any holder with `balance * keepBps >= 1.158e26` (about 11,579 xDAI at 100% keep; 116 xDAI after ten rounds) reverts in `_attach` (`weight * index`) on `setYieldSplit`, deposit and incoming transfer, and once the aggregate `keepWeight` crosses the same line `_donatedYieldAccrued` (`acc * keepWeight`) overflows so `yieldAccrued()`, `claimYield`, `isDistributionReady`, `claimAndDistribute` and `checkUpkeep` all revert. Six-decimal underlyings do not reach the threshold.

