[85] **6. The family path executes a removal that needs zero votes**

`VotingRecipientRegistry.createCrossChainProposal` · Confidence: 85

**Description**
The family path has no zero-threshold guard, so the sole recipient removes itself and the registry stays empty forever on every chain.

`requiredVotes = electorate.length - 1` is 0 for a one-member removal and the proposer's auto-vote satisfies `voteCount >= requiredVotes` on creation. The classic path guards this (`executeProposal` reverts `NotEnoughVotes` when `requiredVotes == 0`; `vote()` auto-executes on `==` only). After execution the local set is empty, every new proposal fails `NotEligibleVoter` (the proposer must be in an empty electorate), the classic add paths are gated `onlyClassicRegistry`, and the owner has no add function. `isDistributionReady()` is false forever, so donated yield already in the vault is never claimable, and the relay replays the same signed payload on every sibling chain. In a two-member family either member first removes the other (threshold 1, satisfied at creation) and then itself.

